{
  "paraphrase": "She is the self-proclaimed clairvoyant daughter of one of Europe’s longest-reigning monarchs; he is a California-based figure who calls himself a sixth-generation shaman. Princess Märtha Louise of Norway’s wedding to Durek Verrett on Saturday afternoon was far from a typical royal event, yet crowds still gathered along the grey, clouded streets of Geiranger to try to see the bride. The 52-year-old, only child of King Harald and Queen Sonja, is fourth in line to the Norwegian throne. She wed the 49-year-old Verrett in a Church of Norway service attended by royals and celebrities at the four-star Hotel Union in a small village overlooking the Geiranger fjord. The princess was accompanied by seven bridesmaids, among them her teenage daughters Leah and Emma Behn from her previous marriage to the late Norwegian writer Ari Behn, which ended in divorce in 2017. Around 350 guests attended, including her brother Crown Prince Haakon and Crown Princess Mette-Marit, Sweden’s Crown Princess Victoria with Prince Daniel, and the Netherlands’ Prince Constantijn and Princess Laurentien. Märtha Louise has long lived outside the usual royal mould, previously saying she is clairvoyant and spending about a decade running a healing school that taught people to communicate with angels. In 2022, she said she would give up official royal responsibilities to concentrate on her and Verrett’s business ventures and to more clearly separate their work from Norway’s royal household. Verrett, who labels himself on Instagram a “servant of God” and an “energy activator,” counts Goop founder Gwyneth Paltrow among his well-known clients and has referred to her as a “soul sister.”"
}
```

